-- title:
--   Reduced Eisenstein torsion bounded by lattice Hecke quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq 2$ and $q \neq p$, and let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $A_q$. Equip $J_0(p) := \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with the module structure over $\mathbb T := \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Nat.Primes})\,\mathbb Z$ given by `heckeModuleBar p`. Then for all natural numbers $k$ and $M$, writing $I = (q^k) + \mathfrak P^M \subseteq \mathbb T$, where $\mathfrak P$ is the contraction along `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal $(q) \subseteq \mathbb Z$, the number of elements of the image under `reductionModL` $A_q\,p$ (reduction of degree-zero divisor classes along the residue map of $A_q$) of the submodule of elements of $J_0(p)$ annihilated by every element of $I$ is at most the number of elements of the quotient of the lattice Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^{\mathrm L} :=$ `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` — the image of the weight-two level-$p$ Hecke algebra in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z}(\mathrm{intLattice}\ p\ 2)$ — by the ideal generated by $q^k$ together with the $M$-th power of the image of $\mathfrak P$ under evaluation of the polynomial generators at the Hecke operators ($U_\ell$ for $\ell \mid p$, $T_\ell$ otherwise) followed by restriction to the lattice algebra. Cardinalities are natural-number cardinalities.
--
--   This is the cyclicity half of Mazur's comparison between the reduced Eisenstein $(q^k,\mathfrak P^M)$-torsion of $J_0(p)$ and the corresponding quotient of the lattice Hecke algebra (Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Chapter II). It is the upper bound used in the subsequent determination of the order of this torsion subgroup as a product of the lattice Hecke quotient with the group of classes on which inertia at $q$ acts through the cyclotomic character.
